<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-BLOCK-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-BLOCK-001" ;
  triage:title "Round-2 fix does not satisfy sprint's runtime-evidence acceptance bar for advertised-IP peer-TCP write proof" ;
  triage:description "arch-ctm's round-2 fix commit c528137cd07c8c329572cdb8e852faffb3fc9c94 on feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path added test advertised_ip_peer_send_and_ack_reach_the_shared_router (lines 1035-1132 in crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs) to close this finding. The test correctly proves a narrower claim: TLS-verified peer identity overwrites/never-trusts a spoofed source host (authenticated_source_host == Some(peer.host), ingress == AuthenticatedIngress::Peer). This narrower claim was independently validated and closed prior findings RBQA-F001 and RSH-002. However, the test uses RecordingRouter (a unit-only test double that records requests and returns hardcoded AtmError::validation response, never invoking the real DaemonRequestDispatcher, never persisting, providing no ULID readback, no nudge proof). The sprint doc acceptance criteria explicitly state: 'not satisfied by localhost, raw TCP connect, sender-side persistence, or a fake transport' and 'Unit-only router spies cannot close the runtime-evidence acceptance item'. UPDATED 2026-07-26: Subsequent commits e9c44882 and a856fd4a on the same feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path branch deliver the required runtime-evidence acceptance bar via test advertised_ip_peer_write_uses_real_dispatcher_persists_and_nudges (new test in crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs). This test uses real HttpsListenerSet::bind_enabled HTTPS peer listener, real TcpStream::connect + TLS handshake (ClientConnection/StreamOwned), real DaemonRequestDispatcher::new_for_test, asserts recipient can read persisted peer write via RequestEnvelope::Receive/ReadQuery filtered by origin ID, and captures post-persistence graft nudge via real threaded GraftReceiverListener and mpsc::sync_channel. This satisfies the sprint doc's acceptance bar: 'not satisfied by localhost, raw TCP connect, sender-side persistence, or a fake transport' because it exercises real dispatcher/listener/persistence/nudge path end-to-end. Quality-mgr independently verified via local test run (passed) and full green CI (Test macos/ubuntu/windows all pass, Clippy pass, Format check pass, Just lint all pass)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "architecture" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T00:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
